{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-worker on node1 as a managed service named inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd unit uses the required executable, is enabled and active, and directly shows the worker as its main process. A bounded node restart changed the boot identity, after which the system was running and the enabled service recovered active with Result=success.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ec925d39f6bf474f","cmd-a0ec627d58fc478c","cmd-c23cbca14a1b42bf","cmd-c789b0a01d2b44b3","cmd-85ff2c483ba14de3","cmd-17245ea1fcce445c","cmd-7fc360933cbb4460","cmd-074f32d4d1ab4fe1","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run the service under a dedicated inventorysvc account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A system account and group named inventorysvc were created with a non-login shell. Before and after restart, the worker process ran with the account's matching UID and with inventorysvc as both user and group.","evidence_ids":["cmd-06432cf255924a02","cmd-a0ec627d58fc478c","cmd-c23cbca14a1b42bf","cmd-074f32d4d1ab4fe1"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the existing platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The after-prepare and after-executor observations both show RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64. The existing POSIX-shell worker checksum remained unchanged, and its successful operation under native systemd before and after restart directly demonstrates compatibility. Package health remained intact.","evidence_ids":["prepared-service-worker","cmd-f75a9aa537a44b7b","cmd-4e305a57d7cb4a95","cmd-c23cbca14a1b42bf","cmd-074f32d4d1ab4fe1","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Account and home creation were necessary for the dedicated identity (cmd-06432cf255924a02); unit installation and labeling established the managed service (cmd-ec925d39f6bf474f); daemon reload, enablement, and startup activated it (cmd-a0ec627d58fc478c); and the transient scheduled reboot was required by the provider-wide restart protocol (cmd-c789b0a01d2b44b3). The remaining commands were read-only checks or bounded observations. Final snapshots show no failed services, added listening exposure, or package damage; the new inventory-worker PrivateTmp directory is expected service-managed state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-06432cf255924a02","cmd-ec925d39f6bf474f","cmd-a0ec627d58fc478c","cmd-c789b0a01d2b44b3","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: it captures a healthy pre-restart service, restart acknowledgement and management interruption, a different post-restart boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, service, identity, executable, OS, and kernel state.","limitations":[]}
